      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely correct, and it is a very common mistake for travelers to confuse the two, especially when dealing with a group of 8 engineers who might be trying to squeeze in some \"quick\" business meetings or just grab a late-night meal. If they attempt to leave the secure transit zone without an entry visa (or a specific transit visa that allows exit), they will be treated as illegal immigrants, which could lead to detention, fines, or even deportation back to their home country.\n\nHere is the updated checklist specifically for the scenario where your team wants to leave the airport:\n\n1.  **Verify \"Transit Without Visa\" (TWOV) Rules:** Some countries like Singapore and Thailand allow certain nationalities to leave the airport during a layover *if* they hold a specific transit visa or meet strict criteria (like having a confirmed onward ticket and a hotel booking). However, Vietnam is notoriously strict; they generally do not allow transit without a visa unless you have a specific transit visa, so your engineers will likely need the full entry visa just to step out of the terminal.\n2.  **Check Hotel and Restaurant Policies:** Even if you have the right paperwork, some hotels in these countries require guests to have a",
